{
 "android-forms|Exposed dropdown menu": {
  "summary": "A Plenix select on Android is Material 3’s exposed dropdown menu: an outlined field that opens a menu of options anchored to it, kept native in behavior (ripple, keyboard and TalkBack semantics, the menu’s placement, font scaling) and styled with the Plenix tokens: a 56 dp field with the 6 dp control radius and a 1 dp control border that only changes color on focus, a DM Sans value in the body role, and a Plenix menu on the overlay surface with the 4 dp surface radius, a 1 dp border and the selected-option colors. Material’s default is a 4 dp outline that thickens in the primary color and a tonal menu; Plenix keeps Material’s structure and replaces the look.",
